# Self-driving reports, scouts, and artifacts

## Report (`system.signal_reports`)

Reports contain findings, research summaries, and impact metrics for a project.
Deleted reports are excluded. Task read access is required.

### Columns

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_reports') }}

## Report artifact (`system.signal_report_artifacts`)

Artifacts record findings, judgments, notes, and work on a report.
Deleted reports and staff-only ranking scores are excluded. Task read access is required.

### Columns

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_report_artifacts') }}

### Relationships

Join `report_id` to `system.signal_reports.id`.
Artifacts are log entries. For the current judgment, use the latest entry of that type by `created_at`.

### Example

```sql
SELECT r.id, r.title, r.status, a.type, a.content, a.created_at
FROM system.signal_reports AS r
JOIN system.signal_report_artifacts AS a ON a.report_id = r.id
ORDER BY a.created_at DESC
LIMIT 20
```

## Report action (`system.signal_report_actions`)

One row per report, user, and action type. Repeated actions update the count and timestamps.
The count is approximate. This table is not an event log.
Task read access is required. Deleted reports are excluded.

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_report_actions') }}

## Report check (`system.signal_report_checks`)

Checks record claims about report outcomes, their schedules, and their latest verdicts.
Task read access is required. Deleted reports are excluded.

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_report_checks') }}

## Report pull request (`system.signal_report_pull_requests`)

Pull request records include state, review decisions, and merge timestamps.
Join `id` to `system.signal_report_artifacts.pull_request_id`.
Task read access is required. Only records linked to visible report artifacts are included.

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_report_pull_requests') }}

## Legacy report assignment (`system.signal_report_assignments`)

Assignments record legacy ownership and pull request links. Current work appears in report artifacts.
Join `report_id` to `system.signal_reports.id`.
Task read access is required. Deleted reports are excluded.

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_report_assignments') }}

## Legacy report task (`system.signal_report_tasks`)

These rows link reports to research or implementation tasks.
Join `report_id` to `system.signal_reports.id`.
Internal research tasks may be absent from `system.tasks`.
Task read access is required. Deleted reports are excluded.

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_report_tasks') }}

## Scout configuration (`system.signal_scout_configs`)

Scout configurations contain schedules, status, and execution settings.
Scout read access is required for all scout tables.
Query scout tables from the parent project environment that owns the scout data.

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_scout_configs') }}

## Scout run (`system.signal_scout_runs`)

Runs record the skill version, summary, emitted findings, and authored or edited reports.
Join `scout_config_id` to `system.signal_scout_configs.id`.
Internal task runs may be absent from `system.task_runs`.

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_scout_runs') }}

## Scout emission (`system.signal_scout_emissions`)

One row per finding emission. Repeated finding identifiers produce separate rows.
Join `scout_run_id` to `system.signal_scout_runs.id`.

{{ schema_columns('system.signal_scout_emissions') }}

## Task artifact (`system.task_artifacts`)

Living artifacts include files, documents, and Slack deliverables with stable version histories.
Join `task_id` to `system.tasks.id` and `task_run_id` to `system.task_runs.id`.
Task read access is required. Private, unfiled, and internal tasks are excluded.

{{ schema_columns('system.task_artifacts') }}

## Additional query examples

```sql
SELECT r.id, r.title, c.status, c.last_outcome, c.next_run_at
FROM system.signal_reports AS r
JOIN system.signal_report_checks AS c ON c.report_id = r.id
ORDER BY c.next_run_at
LIMIT 20
```

```sql
SELECT r.id, r.skill_name, e.finding_id, e.description, e.emitted_at
FROM system.signal_scout_runs AS r
JOIN system.signal_scout_emissions AS e ON e.scout_run_id = r.id
ORDER BY e.emitted_at DESC
LIMIT 20
```
